## TwinCAT MCP (server `twincat`)

- Start every session with `tc_doctor`; if `xae_running` is empty, open the solution in XAE first.
- Live values: `ads_read` (whole FB/struct trees), `ads_leaves <program>` for everything under a program,
  `ads_dump` for a full snapshot to file. Never guess a value — read it.
- Code questions: `proj_resolve_symbol` → `proj_get_code` → `proj_references` / `proj_call_graph`;
  `wf_debug_symbol` does the whole chain in one call.
- Timing questions: `rec_start` (change mode, 1 ms) while the machine runs, then `rec_stats`,
  `rec_pulses`, `rec_latency`; `ads_watch` only for ≤ 60 s one-offs.
- FB validation: `test_scenario` with a parallel recording; port stable scenarios to TcUnit via
  `tcunit_scaffold`.
- Edits: prefer `xae_pou_set` when XAE is open (keeps LineIds), `proj_set_code` otherwise; then
  `xae_build` and read the error items. Deliver code as .TcPOU/.TcDUT/.TcGVL or PLCopen XML.
- Deploy only via `xae_deploy` after `wf_release_check`; then `proj_vs_runtime` must be clean.
- Writes go through the allow/deny lists; do not write to `AT %I*` inputs or safety symbols.
- Library FBs/types: `infosys_declaration <name>` before using one; `infosys_search_code` for a
  known-good call pattern. TwinCAT 3 docs only; do not quote TwinCAT 2 material.
- Every mutating call is audited (`tc_audit_tail`). Say which recording/snapshot ids you produced.
